# Backend Study Guide

* Prioritize concepts over edge cases.
* Understand the architecture and reasoning before coding.
* Implement a clean, consistent solution before optimizing.
* In Controllers:

  * Validate raw input (presence and type).
  * Normalize once into canonical values.
  * Validate business rules on canonical values.
  * Pass only canonical values to the Service.
* Reject common invalid input; ignore rare edge cases unless requirements explicitly demand them.
* Keep the same validation pattern across all controllers and modules.
* Prefer readable, maintainable, and consistent code over perfect code.
* A feature is complete when the design is sound, the implementation is consistent, and the core endpoint tests pass.

